# Keeps the build context to the source. Without this, `docker build .` uploads 1.4 GB of
# node_modules — which would also be the wrong node_modules: pnpm's is symlinks into a content
# store, and CLAUDE.md's rule is that it is never copied into an image. Every image below installs
# from the lockfile instead.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Images build their own; a host artefact copied in would be from a different
# platform and a different moment.
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Never in an image, and .env especially never: §12.5.3 puts secrets in a SOPS-encrypted bootstrap
# file and then OpenBao, not in a layer that anyone who can pull the image can read.
.env
**/.env
.git
.github
docs
design
**/*.md
!config/seed/README.md
